=0A=
>And for the malicious user that, knowing the server is currently in debug=
=0A=
>mode and returning extended errors, can more easily perform attacks on it.=
..=0A=
=0A=
If there's someone on the Internet who can scan every TLS server on the pla=
net=0A=
once a minute to see a brief debug window open up, and then perform somethi=
ng=0A=
like a million-message-attack using a single debug message, then they're ki=
nda=0A=
wasting their abilities in attacking TLS servers...=0A=
